// The summary ends with the number of checks the tests made, `@expect`s and `@require`s,
// held or not, in the test or in a fn it calls: here 5, 3, 2 up to the `@require` that
// ended its test, and 2 before a skip. A test reports its checks as it ends, so one whose
// process ends in another way, by a panic, also one it must make, or by exiting, adds
// none: the last three made 4 that aren't counted. A test that exits by itself, even with
// 0, failed: it never said what it checked.
//# $ ctxc test .
//# exit: 1
//# stdout:
//| ./t.ctx:18: fail: two_of_three_hold: XS[1] == 1: 2 == 1
//| ./t.ctx:24: fail: ends_at_its_second: required: XS[1] == 1: 2 == 1
//| ./t.ctx:28: skip: skips_after_two: its two checks are counted
//| ./t.ctx:1:49: fail: panics_after_two: panic: index 3 out of bounds for length 3
//| ./t.ctx:45: fail: leaves_after_one: its process ended with exit code 0
//| tests: 7 run, 2 passed, 4 failed, 1 skipped, 0 not selected, 12 checks

